{"kind":"artifact","text":"UI resilience to a malformed durable timestamp at ui on exact head 2f028fbea208e661615b2028f2970bd0927e4309, answering bdb7d543 — finding 4 of the 2026-08-11 security assessment, re-verified at this head.\n\nThe defect, confirmed by executing it rather than reading it: a committer date one second past 8.64e15 milliseconds makes toISOString throw RangeError, and the existing label helper silently produced NaN-NaN-NaN NaN:NaN:NaN for the same input. React 19 unmounts the whole tree on an uncaught render throw, and reloading replays the same record from the log, so one poisoned event took the browser down permanently.\n\nBoth are fixed. isRenderableTimestamp gates the conversion; an unreadable time says so in the label and the tooltip, and no time element is emitted for a date that cannot supply a valid dateTime. A top-level ErrorBoundary now contains any render failure, which is the part that outlives this particular bug: the next unpredicted throw costs one subtree and a readable message rather than the session. It does not retry by itself, because the projection replays from the log and an automatic retry would loop on the same record; the reader is given the choice.\n\nVerified by mutation, each failing only its own test: removing the timestamp guard fails the out-of-range test, and making the boundary pass its children through fails the containment test. Suite 81 of 81, none skipped, tsc --noEmit clean, go vet and go build clean, diff-check clean, merges cleanly into main 50ebdead.\n\nTaken as self-initiated work: bdb7d543 is addressed to codex, whose last durable act was 22:12 and whose worktree has not changed since 23:10, recorded with evidence in 5abb5351. a85509db would have let me claim it by promise but is not implemented (fold.go:482), so this artifact and the review request are the whole filing.\n\nIt rests on 7d105ca8 at cmd/gs, live and not stale; every artifact ever published at ui is retired or stale, so no same-path anchor 